#lang saffron
;; saffron-lang-plan D7: a region bracket in a Saffron file is refused, and
;; the reason is that it would SILENTLY DO NOTHING -- not that it would be
;; unsafe.
;;
;; A region rewinds a generation only when a static walk over the bracket's
;; RESULT TYPE proves nothing outside it still points in.  Over `any` that
;; walk clears nothing (region_type_reaches_node's `default: return true`
;; arm), so the emitter takes the conservative branch and RETIRES the
;; generation: plain `tur_region_pop` where the same program in Turmeric
;; emits `tur_region_pop_checked`.  Measured, on the emitted C.
;;
;; So the bracket is safe and reclaims nothing.  That is the silent downgrade
;; D7 refuses: the cost is paid, the saving never arrives, and without this
;; diagnostic nothing says so.
;;
;; The rejection is keyed on the RESOLVED binding, not the spelling, and is
;; placed after the let-alias resolution in elab_call.c -- so `(let [g
;; with-region] (g thunk))` is caught too, and a local genuinely named
;; `with-region` that is not the stdlib defn is not.
;;
;; `bt-scope` opens a region as well and is deliberately NOT refused: its
;; feature is the trail level, which works in Saffron unchanged, and only the
;; region half degrades.  Taking a working feature away to report a lost
;; optimisation is the wrong trade.

(defn mk [n] (with-region (fn [] (+ n 1))))

(defn main []
  (println (cast (mk 4) int))
  0)
